# {{LOOP_NAME}} — Trigger Definition

> This file is the host-agnostic launch contract for the loop. It specifies
> what the loop is trying to achieve, where its state lives, and exactly how
> to start a run — with a Claude Code one-liner and a plain fallback that
> works on any platform.

---

## Verifiable goal

The loop stops when this predicate holds:

> **{{GOAL}}**

Every run must check this predicate after the verifier passes. If it holds,
the loop writes a final summary to the state file and exits cleanly.

---

## State file

```
{{STATE_PATH}}
```

Every run reads this file at startup and writes it before stopping. If the
file is missing or empty, treat it as a first run and initialize the ledger
before taking any action.

---

## Launch prompt

Pass this prompt verbatim when starting the loop manually or via a scheduler:

> Read the loop's `CONTRACT.md`, `{{STATE_PATH}}`, and `log.md`, plus the
> loop's `SKILL.md`, then run one iteration of the {{LOOP_NAME}} loop.

That is the host-agnostic fallback. It works on any platform that can load a
skill file and read markdown files — no host-specific tooling required. The
three files (`CONTRACT.md`, `{{STATE_PATH}}`, `log.md`) are the loop's entire
memory; the prompt must name all of them so a cold start recovers fully.

---

## How to start

### Claude Code (built-in `/loop` and `/schedule` skills)

Self-paced, run-until-done — the default fit for a goal-predicate loop
(`/loop <prompt>` with no interval):

```
/loop Read the loop's CONTRACT.md, {{STATE_PATH}}, and log.md, plus the loop's SKILL.md, then run one iteration of the {{LOOP_NAME}} loop.
```

To poll on a fixed cadence instead, put an interval before the prompt
(`/loop <interval> <prompt>`):

```
/loop 10m Read the loop's CONTRACT.md, {{STATE_PATH}}, and log.md, plus the loop's SKILL.md, then run one iteration of the {{LOOP_NAME}} loop.
```

For an unattended recurring run in the cloud, use `/schedule` to create a
cron-scheduled routine with the same launch prompt.

`/loop` and `/schedule` are built-in Claude Code skills, but their syntax can
change between versions — verify against your installed version's docs. See
`references/host-adapters.md` for the current Claude Code mechanics.

### Other hosts

For non-Claude hosts, verify scheduling/loop mechanics against that host's
current docs before scaffolding — then wire the launch prompt below into its
scheduler or runner.

### Fallback (host-agnostic — works on any platform)

```
Read the loop's CONTRACT.md, {{STATE_PATH}}, and log.md, plus the loop's SKILL.md, then run one iteration of the {{LOOP_NAME}} loop.
```

Paste this as the opening prompt in any agent session. The loop's `SKILL.md`
contains all logic; `CONTRACT.md`, `{{STATE_PATH}}`, and `log.md` contain all
state. No additional tooling is needed.

---

## Trigger notes

- **Gate G0 comes first.** Do not fire any trigger until a human has reviewed
  and approved `CONTRACT.md` — the contract, not the build, is what a human
  signs off on. Confirm G0 is cleared in `HUMAN-GATES.md` before the first
  live run.
- Before enabling any automated trigger, confirm the remaining gates in
  `HUMAN-GATES.md` — G1 (pre-run sign-off) and G2 (non-convergence: N
  consecutive verifier failures) — are in place and that the approver is
  reachable. An ordinary red build does NOT page a human; restart within
  budget instead.
- The budget / stop limits in `HUMAN-GATES.md` take precedence over any
  scheduler interval. If the loop hits its iteration or cost cap, it halts
  regardless of how often the trigger fires.
- Trigger syntax above is current for Claude Code at authoring time — verify
  against current host docs before relying on it.
